1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,203
A mountain stream can
flood a village in hours,

2
00:00:02,253 --> 00:00:03,420
often at night.

3
00:00:03,470 --> 00:00:04,684
The forecast sees it coming.

4
00:00:04,734 --> 00:00:06,472
The village never hears it.

5
00:00:06,522 --> 00:00:07,874
That's Pukaar.

6
00:00:08,074 --> 00:00:10,456
On the night of 30 June 2025,

7
00:00:10,506 --> 00:00:12,109
cloudbursts hit Mandi district:

8
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:14,588
at least 10 dead, 34 missing.

9
00:00:14,638 --> 00:00:16,926
Forecasts exist, but they
are numbers on a website,

10
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:18,535
not a warning anyone hears.

11
00:00:18,585 --> 00:00:19,703
Pukaar turns a forecast

12
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:20,871
into a spoken Hindi alert

13
00:00:20,921 --> 00:00:22,764
on every phone in the village.

14
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:24,908
A district officer approves it in one tap,

15
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:27,235
and villagers confirm they heard it.

16
00:00:27,935 --> 00:00:29,098
Here's Gohar, in Mandi,

17
00:00:29,148 --> 00:00:30,077
July 2023,

18
00:00:30,127 --> 00:00:32,175
replayed through Pukaar's real rules.

19
00:00:32,225 --> 00:00:34,762
The river forecast passes
its own 90th percentile:

20
00:00:34,812 --> 00:00:35,710
Watch.

21
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:37,949
Rain passes 64.5 millimetres

22
00:00:37,999 --> 00:00:38,830
with the river high:

23
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:39,909
Warning.

24
00:00:39,959 --> 00:00:41,584
Then 115.6:

25
00:00:41,634 --> 00:00:42,649
Critical.

26
00:00:43,099 --> 00:00:43,895
72 hours

27
00:00:43,945 --> 00:00:45,609
before the river's peak day.

28
00:00:45,659 --> 00:00:48,259
Now the same night, running live on AWS.

29
00:00:48,309 --> 00:00:49,331
Every 15 minutes,

30
00:00:49,381 --> 00:00:50,615
EventBridge wakes a Lambda

31
00:00:50,665 --> 00:00:52,398
that sets each village's level by rule,

32
00:00:52,448 --> 00:00:53,697
never by a model.

33
00:00:53,747 --> 00:00:55,783
The officer on duty sees the Hindi draft.

34
00:00:55,832 --> 00:00:57,196
Step Functions has paused,

35
00:00:57,246 --> 00:00:58,772
waiting for one tap.

36
00:00:58,822 --> 00:01:00,479
The model only fills a fixed template,

37
00:01:00,529 --> 00:01:02,006
and a checker rejects any number

38
00:01:02,056 --> 00:01:03,719
not in the decision trace.

39
00:01:03,769 --> 00:01:06,082
Code has already chosen the
level and the recipients;

40
00:01:06,132 --> 00:01:08,211
the officer only decides to send.

41
00:01:08,261 --> 00:01:09,351
Approve.

42
00:01:10,351 --> 00:01:12,346
Amazon Polly speaks it in Hindi:

43
00:01:18,446 --> 00:01:19,704
Every phone gets the voice

44
00:01:19,754 --> 00:01:20,978
and one button:

45
00:01:21,028 --> 00:01:21,851
मिल गया, got it.

46
00:01:21,901 --> 00:01:26,463
Pukaar times each alert, from the river
rising to the first person who heard it.

47
00:01:26,513 --> 00:01:27,108
In a replay,

48
00:01:27,158 --> 00:01:28,852
it goes to test phones only.

49
00:01:28,902 --> 00:01:30,676
Every decision lands in an audit log:

50
00:01:30,726 --> 00:01:32,562
Cedar allowed the officer's approval,

51
00:01:32,612 --> 00:01:34,535
and refused a village pradhan who tried,

52
00:01:34,585 --> 00:01:37,014
with the policy and the reason.

53
00:01:37,064 --> 00:01:39,370
Villagers report back
by voice, photo or text,

54
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,374
from any phone, even offline.

55
00:01:41,424 --> 00:01:42,398
On slow 3G,

56
00:01:42,448 --> 00:01:44,999
the page is ready in 4.6 seconds.

57
00:01:45,999 --> 00:01:48,347
The whole loop is serverless on AWS.

58
00:01:48,397 --> 00:01:50,763
EventBridge Scheduler
runs the sweep Lambda,

59
00:01:50,813 --> 00:01:53,301
with no retries and a dead-letter queue.

60
00:01:53,351 --> 00:01:54,544
One DynamoDB table,

61
00:01:54,594 --> 00:01:55,605
with conditional writes,

62
00:01:55,655 --> 00:01:57,651
so an alert is never sent twice.

63
00:01:57,701 --> 00:01:59,426
Step Functions waits for the officer;

64
00:01:59,476 --> 00:02:01,468
no answer moves to the next one.

65
00:02:01,518 --> 00:02:02,967
Bedrock drafts through Strands,

66
00:02:03,017 --> 00:02:03,756
Polly speaks,

67
00:02:03,806 --> 00:02:05,597
and the audio lands in S3.

68
00:02:05,647 --> 00:02:06,622
Telegram delivers it,

69
00:02:06,672 --> 00:02:09,172
and the tap comes back
through API Gateway.

70
00:02:09,222 --> 00:02:11,635
Cognito signs officers in,
Cedar checks every action,

71
00:02:11,685 --> 00:02:13,855
and 9 CloudWatch alarms watch it all.

72
00:02:13,905 --> 00:02:14,655
This is live:

73
00:02:14,705 --> 00:02:16,452
53 approval workflows so far,

74
00:02:16,502 --> 00:02:17,963
45 succeeded.

75
00:02:18,013 --> 00:02:19,697
Polly's Hindi audio in S3,

76
00:02:19,747 --> 00:02:20,656
and the health check,

77
00:02:20,706 --> 00:02:21,760
right now.

78
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:23,376
Nothing runs between requests:

79
00:02:23,426 --> 00:02:25,498
no servers, no database instance.

80
00:02:25,548 --> 00:02:27,002
In our 2025 back-test,

81
00:02:27,052 --> 00:02:30,080
the global forecasts missed
the Mandi cloudburst.

82
00:02:30,130 --> 00:02:31,440
So a verified villager report

83
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:33,293
can raise a level on its own.

84
00:02:33,343 --> 00:02:35,171
And replay lead times are an upper bound:

85
00:02:35,221 --> 00:02:37,272
real forecasts are less certain.

86
00:02:37,322 --> 00:02:38,595
The river will still rise.

87
00:02:38,645 --> 00:02:40,445
Now the village hears first.
